// The two request paths, drawn with HTML so it scales, reads in both themes and stays text for screen readers.
---
<figure class="arch" aria-labelledby="arch-caption">
	<div class="arch-head"><strong>Two request paths</strong><span>conceptual</span></div>

	<div class="node"><strong>Network devices</strong><small>NAS · access points · switches · BNG</small></div>
	<div class="link" aria-hidden="true">↓ UDP · RadSec · DTLS · TCP</div>

	<div class="row two">
		<div class="node"><strong>RADIUS server A</strong><small>validate · authenticate</small></div>
		<div class="node"><strong>RADIUS server B</strong><small>validate · authenticate</small></div>
	</div>

	<div class="row split">
		<div class="path">
			<div class="link" aria-hidden="true">↙ authentication</div>
			<div class="node plain"><strong>Identity stores</strong><small>users file · SQL · LDAP/AD · Netlogon · home servers</small></div>
			<p class="note">Decided on the RADIUS server; keeps working without a cluster majority, except shared-state features.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="path">
			<div class="link" aria-hidden="true">↘ accounting</div>
			<div class="cluster">
				<div class="cluster-head"><strong>Replicated log</strong><span>3 members</span></div>
				<div class="row three">
					<div class="node"><strong>Member 1</strong></div>
					<div class="node"><strong>Member 2</strong></div>
					<div class="node"><strong>Member 3</strong></div>
				</div>
				<p class="note">fsync on a majority, then the Accounting-Response.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="link" aria-hidden="true">↓ committed records</div>
			<div class="node plain"><strong>Exports</strong><small>PostgreSQL · JSON lines · RADIUS forwarding</small></div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<figcaption id="arch-caption">
		Accounting is answered only after the commit; delivery to an export is a separate, later step.{' '}
		<a href="/docs/reliability/accounting-contract/">Read the contract →</a>
	</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.arch {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 1rem;
		background: var(--color-surface);
		box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgb(40 37 29 / 0.06);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
	.arch-head, .cluster-head {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: var(--color-text-faint);
	}
	.arch-head strong { color: var(--color-text); }
	.cluster-head { color: var(--color-primary); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
	.node {
		padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 0.4rem;
		background: var(--color-bg);
		text-align: center;
	}
	.node strong { display: block; color: var(--color-text); font-size: 0.86rem; }
	.node small { display: block; margin-top: 0.15rem; color: var(--color-text-faint); font-size: 0.74rem; line-height: 1.35; }
	.plain { background: var(--color-surface-2); }
	.row { display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; }
	.two { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
	.three { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
	.split { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.35fr; align-items: start; gap: 0.9rem; }
	.link {
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		min-height: 2rem;
		color: var(--color-text-faint);
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-size: 0.74rem;
	}
	.cluster {
		padding: 0.75rem;
		border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 35%, transparent);
		border-radius: 0.6rem;
		background: var(--color-primary-tint);
	}
	.cluster .node { background: var(--color-surface); padding: 0.45rem 0.3rem; }
	.note { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text-faint); font-size: 0.74rem; line-height: 1.4; }
	figcaption {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		padding-top: 0.8rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
		color: var(--color-text-faint);
		font-size: 0.78rem;
	}
	figcaption a { color: var(--color-primary); }
	@media (max-width: 30rem) {
		.split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
	}
</style>
